# No intent crutches

CodeForge’s agent must work from a stable **tool + system contract**, not from hardcoded intent detection.

## Forbidden

- Rewriting the user message with “Harness note” / apply / continue enrichers based on phrase matchers
- Regex (or similar) sniffers on user or assistant text to decide the model “meant apply / corrija / I’ll fix”
- Soft coaching nudges injected as fake `user` turns (“you narrated without tools”, “thin final”, “stuck — try edit”)
- Growing matchers for Portuguese/English synonyms instead of fixing tools or the system prompt

Portuguese/English regexes are allowed only as **matchers of user input** where the product must recognize locale (see `english-texts.mdc`), not to drive agent behavior.

## Allowed (structural)

- System prompt and tool schemas that state how to work (`edit` workflow, no prose-only patches)
- Tool-result feedback (`Already applied`, `old_string was not found`, failed-repeat refusal)
- Execution gates: `readThisTurn`, edit fingerprint block, stage/path refusals
- Protocol events: length truncation, invalid tool JSON, step-budget / hard stuck wrap, oracle red

## When the model only describes a fix

Do **not** add a new trigger. Improve the contract (system/`edit` description) or the tool loop so calling tools is the natural path. Leave the failure visible rather than papering over it with matchers.
